nodecode-kame-rotate is a rewrite of Kame696's Kame696/kame-api-rotation-for-hermes:

  https://github.com/Kame696/kame-api-rotation-for-hermes
  commit 5e4a12f249f679ae5dcbf0d22e4ffbfeba4e5e2b
  MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 KAME (https://github.com/Kame696) (LICENSE)

Rewritten: the provider half of KAME, in Python a plugin that re-registers
Hermes' own provider profiles with two extra client factories, becomes one
Common Lisp cell that keeps the same promise as verbs. The pool, the ordering
it is tried in, and the reading of a refusal are reimplemented from the
original's companion plugin (hermes-kame-api-rotation): a 429 honouring
Retry-After, a 401 or 403 taken as a wrong key rather than a busy one, a 5xx
taken as a busy endpoint, each key sitting out before it is asked again, and
any other 4xx answered as the call's own failure with the endpoint's words.
The wire is one OpenAI-compatible /chat/completions POST; the keys are read
from the environment variables a config section names.

Left out: the in-process replacement of every provider profile, which a
Nodecode cell has no seam for — Nodecode's provider lanes build their own
clients, so the rewrite exposes the rotation as two tools and a command
instead of wrapping the harness. Also left out: the companion plugin's
dashboard, its per-home key store and its env-file syncing, which describe
Hermes' own state; and the Anthropic Messages and Responses wires, since one
OpenAI-compatible wire carries the pool's whole behaviour.
